// ML-KEM (FIPS 203) decapsulation known-answer vectors.
//
// ACVP vectors are "decapsulation" VAL cases (2 "valid decapsulation" and
// 2 "modified ciphertext" per parameter set) from the NIST ACVP-Server
// repository at commit 15c0f3deeefbfa8cb6cd32a99e1ca3b738c66bf0:
// https://github.com/usnistgov/ACVP-Server/blob/15c0f3deeefbfa8cb6cd32a99e1ca3b738c66bf0/gen-val/json-files/ML-KEM-encapDecap-FIPS203/internalProjection.json
// The "modified ciphertext" cases carry the official expected output of the
// FIPS 203 implicit rejection path: k = J(z || c).
//
// The "strcmp" vectors are from C2SP/CCTV (CC0); their re-encrypted
// ciphertext comparison contains early zero bytes that trip
// short-circuiting comparisons:
// https://github.com/C2SP/CCTV/blob/main/ML-KEM/strcmp/ML-KEM-512.txt (and 768/1024)

